Z||000012||flexableface||09-21-2000||02:40 PM||||yeah i was wondering about that yellow dash. i really like the way it looks and i was think about painting mine. If i did do this i would probably want to pull out the dash correct? And if i do have to pull the dash how hard is it to pull it out? thanks Luke||||reg||5
Z||000013||HugGRRRFiero||09-21-2000||03:54 PM||||Pull the dash... it's not too hard to do.  <P>Tools you'll need:<BR>* 7mm & 10mm 1/4 sockets, extention and wrench<BR>* Phillips & flat head screwdrivers<BR>* A Torx bit screwdriver or socket for the dash pod cover<P>First, you'll need to remove the shift and radio consoles, a metal plate behind the radio console.  The four console screws are located under the cigarette trays to get that started.  Second, remove the dash pod cover and hood release lever.  Next, carefully pull the speaker covers to uncover the screws that hold the upper part of the dash.  Remove the speakers and disconnect them.  Two screws are on the underside of the dash on the outside corners.  That's about it, takes about 1 hour to do it the first time, about 30 minutes the second time around.  Hope this helps...||||reg||1
Z||000014||HugGRRRFiero||09-21-2000||03:55 PM||||Opps...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by HugGRRRFiero (edited 09-21-2000).]||||reg||1
